  "notes": "Drawn from N1808U (737-8 MAX, left, Dec 2025) and N9007K (Aug 2026). The fin is the Heart fin as measured for the state jets (Lone Star One). From below the bands are seen to cross the aft belly; their exact line under the belly is taken from the sides. The registration and fleet number aren't drawn. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on two 737-800s (N8524Z, N8315C) fitted to the measured 737-800 shape: the sweep's six edges re-measured as curves (smooth), about 0.6-1 m further forward than first drawn, meeting the belly where the side view shows them; the fin redrawn from the photos (the yellow band runs the whole leading edge, the red covers the rest, the blue is only a small lower aft triangle), its x read as shares of the photo's chord at each height because the measured shape's fin is narrower than the photos'. Titles' lengths measured; 'Southwest.com' on the engines on every photo but N8524Z's 2026 one (a swapped cowl?).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The Heart livery replaced Canyon Blue (2001–2014); the last Canyon Blue 737-700s were repainted or retired by the early 2020s."
}
